## Ruling

Design §6.4 requires compliance rate over the FIRST 100 LIVE invocations under
real agent load, explicitly "not synthetic eval set" — generating 100 synthetic
invocations to force closure would violate the task's own definition. The 18
existing invocations are dev acceptance traffic (Tasks 10/11), not production load.

- Register: Workhorse stays PROVISIONAL (unchanged entry, conditions already
  recorded there; expiry 2026-10-06 unaffected).
- Re-review TRIGGER: cumulative 100 live workhorse invocations (expected during
  beta) — re-run this telemetry query, then fire Outcome A or B.
- Checkbox state: telemetry-review + record-numbers boxes ticked; the two
  outcome boxes left UNTICKED (rule 7 — nothing happened to tick).

Early signal (non-binding, n=18): zero schema-validation failures; the only
failures were a transport-encoding defect already fixed and test-pinned.
